<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rogier van der Weyden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1399–1464</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rogier van der Weyden was an Early Netherlandish painter, official painter of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> from 1436. His emotionally intense works, such as the Descent from the Cross now in the Prado and the Last Judgement altarpiece for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hospices-de-beaune">Hospices de Beaune</a>, were widely copied across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. He also painted portraits of the Burgundian court, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rogier-van-der-weyden.jpg" alt="Rogier van der Weyden" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rogier_Lamp_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
